From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The forest past a lower map's south edge on the taller field
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Route 215's maps sit at height 0 in the map matrix, and the scenery map
south of them (the forest, MAP_HEADER_EVERYWHERE) at 4, two tiles
higher. Below the route's ledges its cliffs come down to the route's
south edge (z 608), but not down to the forest's edge, higher up: the
field at the DS's pixel size, with 24 lines more below the DS's, sees
between them there, and the 3D's clear colour showed as a black strip
under the cliff. The DS's view never reaches it from where the player
goes.

A scenery map south of a lower map is drawn once more, 8 tiles north
and 4 tiles below that map (Port_RenderSceneryMapLowered, after its
lowered copies): under that map everywhere, so it isn't seen, and past
that map's edge the forest is seen going on behind and below. It's 16
polygons, sent only when in view; only on the wider field, as the
lowered copies.

---
diff --git a/src/overlay005/land_data.c b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
index 46ebb161..cfccff9a 100644
--- a/src/overlay005/land_data.c
+++ b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
@@ -1757,10 +1757,17 @@ static void Port_RenderMirroredEdges(const LandDataManager *landDataMan, ModelAt
 // itself, from the height of the lowest map beside it up, 2 tiles apart:
 // those copies fill the slit as a wall would, under the map itself
 // everywhere else (they're small: 16 polygons each).
+// South of a lower map, the wider field's bottom lines see past that map's
+// south edge, where its cliffs don't come down to this map's edge, higher
+// up: the 3D's clear colour between them (Route 215 below its ledges, z
+// 608, a black strip under the cliff). It's drawn once more, 8 tiles north
+// and 4 tiles below that map: under that map everywhere, and past its edge
+// the forest seen going on behind and below.
 static void Port_RenderSceneryMapLowered(const u8 index, const LandDataManager *landDataMan)
 {
     LoadedMap *loadedMap = landDataMan->loadedMaps[index];
     int width = landDataMan->mapMatrixWidth, mapMatrixIndex = loadedMap->mapMatrixIndex, lowest = 0x7fffffff;
+    int north = 0x7fffffff;   // (the height of the map north of it, if lower)
     u16 matrixID = MapMatrix_GetMatrixID(landDataMan->mapMatrix);
     int matrixWidth = MapMatrix_GetWidth(landDataMan->mapMatrix);
     int altitude = MapMatrix_GetAltitudeAtCoords(landDataMan->mapMatrix, matrixID, mapMatrixIndex % width, mapMatrixIndex / width, matrixWidth);
@@ -1788,6 +1795,10 @@ static void Port_RenderSceneryMapLowered(const u8 index, const LandDataManager *
         if (otherAltitude < altitude && otherAltitude < lowest) {
             lowest = otherAltitude;
         }
+
+        if (dz == -1 && otherAltitude < altitude) {
+            north = otherAltitude;
+        }
     }
 
     if (lowest == 0x7fffffff) {
@@ -1813,6 +1824,17 @@ static void Port_RenderSceneryMapLowered(const u8 index, const LandDataManager *
             Easy3D_DrawRenderObj(&loadedMap->mapRenderObj, &position, &rotationMatrix, &scale);
         }
     }
+
+    // (behind the edge of the lower map north of it: 8 tiles north, 4
+    // tiles below that map)
+    if (north != 0x7fffffff) {
+        position.y = (north - 8) * (MAP_OBJECT_TILE_SIZE / 2) + landDataMan->offset.y;
+        position.z -= 8 * MAP_OBJECT_TILE_SIZE;
+
+        if (GFXBoxTest_IsModelInView(loadedMap->mapRenderObj.resMdl, &position, &rotationMatrix, &scale)) {
+            Easy3D_DrawRenderObj(&loadedMap->mapRenderObj, &position, &rotationMatrix, &scale);
+        }
+    }
 }
 
 static BOOL Port_SceneryMirroredOver(const LandDataManager *landDataMan, u8 index);
